have F4 and J1 which are honors, so not All Simples.  \n- Since I have a pair of F4 (North wind), which is neither prevailing wind (West) nor seat wind (South), no extra points.  \n- I have two identical chows of B6,B7,B8 \u2014 that's a Pure Double Chow (1 point).  \n- If I form a pung of F4 or B5, that could give Pung of Terminals or Honors (1 point) if F4 (honor) pung.  \n\nBut the key is to reach at least 8 total points to win. Currently I have only 1 point (Pure Double Chow) from melds. I need more.  \n\nPossible discards:  \n- Discard T7: removes bamboo, keeps dots and honors, but T7 is a simple tile, not useful for melds currently.  \n- Discard B9: a terminal in dots, but I have only one, not useful.  \n- Discard B5: I have two B5s, discarding one breaks a potential pair/pung.  \n- Discard J1: single dragon, not useful.  \n- Discard B7: I have one B7, but it could be used in a chow with B6,B8? But I already have two B6-B8 chows, and B6/B8 might be scarce.  \n- Discard F4: I have two F4s, discarding one breaks a pair.  \n\nConsidering tile safety:  \n- Next player's history shows they played T9, W7, Chi W2, played B4, W9, B9. They might need dots or characters.  \n- Previous player's history shows they played B1, W3, Chi B2, T1, B7, B7, B2 \u2014 they are active in dots and characters.  \n- Unshown tiles: B5 has 4 left, B7 has 2 left, B9 has 2 left, F4 has 4 left, J1 has 3 left.  \n\nI think keeping the F4 pair is good because it's a potential pung (honor) for points. Keeping B5 pair is also good for potential pung. I have two melds already, so I need two more groups. Best plan is to try to draw into a pung (B5 or F4) or complete a chow with B7 or B9.  \n\nDiscarding T7 seems safe because next player played T9 and W9, not T7; previous player played T1. T7 is a middle tile, relatively safe. Also, by discarding T7, I reduce suits, maybe aiming for One Voided Suit (2 points) if I eventually discard all bamboo? But I only have one bamboo tile (T7), so discarding it leaves only dots and honors, giving One Voided Suit (2 points) if I win with no bamboo. That's a bonus.  \n\nDiscarding B9 might be risky because previous player played B7,B7, and B9 is a terminal dot, maybe someone needs it.  \n\nDiscarding J1 is safe? Dragons are often collected, but J1 has 3 left.  \n\nGiven my hand, I should discard the lone tile that doesn't contribute to potential pairs or melds: T7 is a lone bamboo, not matching my dots melds or honor pairs.  \n\nReason:  \nDiscarding T7 keeps my pairs (F4 and B5) intact, maintains flexibility to draw into pungs or chows in dots, and may help achieve One Voided Suit (2 points) if I avoid bamboo. It also seems relatively safe based on opponents' discards. The hand is still far from winning, but I need to build towards a viable hand with scoring potential.  \n\nAnswer: Play T7"}
